# Exclude archived/legacy code from security scans
archive/

# Exclude Helm charts from filesystem scans
# Helm charts have external dependencies that are fetched at deploy time
# Trivy cannot render templates without these dependencies
# Container images are scanned separately in the container-tests workflow
helm/

# Base OS image CVEs - no upstream fix available
# Review periodically and remove when patches are released
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-15
#
# To populate this section, run Trivy locally against affected images:
#   trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed <service>:scan
# Then add specific CVE IDs below (one per line) for OS-level CVEs that
# have no fix in Debian bookworm / Ubuntu 22.04 base images.
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# npm-bundled tool CVEs (minimatch, tar inside /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm)
# These packages are npm's own INTERNAL dependencies used during package
# management operations, not the application's runtime code.
# The application (NestJS) does not call minimatch or tar directly at runtime;
# they are only reached by npm/npx for the Prisma migration step on startup.
# Accepted risk: these tools are not exposed to untrusted input in production.
# Revisit when npm 11.x ships with minimatch>=10.2.3 and tar>=7.5.11 bundled.
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-29
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# minimatch ReDoS / path-traversal (CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904)
# Affects minimatch 9.0.5 and 10.1.1 bundled inside npm@11.7.0
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# tar path-traversal / symlink / permissions chain (npm@11.7.0 bundles tar 7.5.2)
# Fixed in tar 7.5.3 -> 7.5.11; requires npm to ship updated bundled tar
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
